  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Every Girl in School Year Two Payment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &#x2018;Every Girl in School&#x2019; project in Kajiado and Turkana, Kenya aims to build communities&#x2019; resilience, capabilities and capacity to support girls and reduce social, cultural and environmental barriers to education, together with the implementing partner Girl Child Network. The objectives of the project are for children, especially girls and children with disabilities, from the Maasai and Turkana communities attain inclusive quality primary education that supports the achievement of healthy and fulfilling lives. The key activities include ensuring target schools meet the UNICEF standards of a child-friendly and gender-sensitive school, training children on their rights and protection and gender equality, and the construction of gender and disability inclusive sanitation facilities in target schools.</narrative>
  </description>
